// Darwin answers the unit POSIX leaves open differently from Linux: ru_maxrss is the maximum
// resident set size in BYTES, from the BSD lineage. CORROBORATED BY EXECUTION on the operator's
// macOS 15 machine, not read off the manual alone (2026-08-05): getrusage(RUSAGE_SELF).ru_maxrss
// returned 15417344 for a bare python3 interpreter. As bytes that is 14.7 MiB, an ordinary
// interpreter footprint; as kibibytes it would be 14.7 GiB, absurd on a 16 GiB machine and caught
// by nothing. The discriminating check was the magnitude, recorded because the two readings differ
// by 1024x in the direction that looks survivable.
//
// WHY THIS MATTERS BEYOND TIDINESS: the same divergence makes a single hardwired transport unsafe.
// A portable getrusage call assuming one unit would silently mis-scale every peak-residency fact on
// half the fleet — and peak residency is exactly the input the memory governor sizes admission
// against.

data darwin_rusage_maxrss_unit: RusageMaxrssUnit = MaxrssBytes

data extdeps_model_scope: ExternalModelScope = ExternalModelScope {
